# Auto-resolve merge conflicts for generated files
# The pre-commit hook regenerates ATTESTATION.md anyway, so conflicts don't matter
ATTESTATION.md merge=ours

# CHANGES.md is append-at-top: every ticket branch inserts its entry directly
# under the header, so N concurrent branches conflict, and each merge
# re-conflicts every branch still open.
#
# DO NOT add a merge driver for it. Both obvious ones are wrong:
#
#   * The default 3-way merge produces a resolution that is WRONG but looks
#     right. Entries share the same "**How to run it.**" / "**Rollback.**"
#     headings, so git matches those lines and COLLAPSES two entries into one —
#     deleting the markers then welds one ticket's rollback instructions onto
#     another ticket's entry.
#
#   * `merge=union` was tried here and reverted. It fails more quietly: it keeps
#     every line, so nothing looks missing, but it DROPS the shared context
#     lines — which are exactly the "**How to run it.**" heading and the ```bash
#     fences. Five branches came out with 9 entry headings and 8 run blocks, two
#     of them with an odd number of fences, and one entry's command block
#     belonging to a different ticket. A reviewer caught it; a check for
#     headings and separators did not.
#
# Resolve conflicts with `node scripts/factory/merge-changes.mjs`, which merges
# whole entries instead of lines and then ASSERTS every emitted entry is
# byte-identical to its source. Run `--check` after any merge of this file, by
# any method.
